# 📈 Stock Trading Platform

### CodeAlpha Java Programming Internship – Task 2

A console-based **Stock Trading Platform** developed using Java and Object-Oriented Programming (OOP). This application simulates a basic stock market where users can buy and sell stocks, manage their portfolios, and track their investment performance.

## 📌 About the Project

The Stock Trading Platform is designed to provide a simple simulation of stock trading.

Users can view available stocks, purchase shares, sell owned shares, check their portfolio value, and track profit or loss.

This project was developed as part of my Java Programming Internship at **CodeAlpha**.

## ✨ Features

- 📊 **Market Data:** Display available stocks and their prices.
- 🛒 **Buy Stocks:** Purchase stocks using the available account balance.
- 💰 **Sell Stocks:** Sell owned shares and receive the selling amount.
- 📁 **Portfolio Management:** View stock holdings and quantities.
- 📈 **Performance Tracking:** Calculate total portfolio value and profit or loss.
- 📜 **Transaction History:** View all buying and selling transactions.
- 🔄 **Update Stock Prices:** Simulate changes in market prices.
- ✅ **Input Validation:** Handle invalid stock symbols and quantities.

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- Java
- Object-Oriented Programming (OOP)
- ArrayList
- Scanner Class
- Constructors and Methods
- Loops and Conditional Statements

